{"output":"I'll start by discovering the tools on the `tickets`, `inventory` and `docs` servers, then read the policy documents.\n\nNow inventory: every item (including discontinued) and all adjustments in `returns`.\n\nTotal 32 adjustments in `returns`; I'll read the other pages.\n\nAnalysis done. I'll process the tickets in id order, starting with 1402. Its stock was already cleared, so it only needs the comment and status.\n\nEvery ticket is settled. I'll check that no open `refund` tickets remain, then write the status file.\n\nMy summary counts were off (20 refunded, 5 not refundable), so I'll correct the file.\n\nI settled all 27 open `refund` tickets in id order, and a final search shows none left open. `/app/STATUS.json` is written with status `success`.\n\nI applied the 2026-07 refund policy, the 2026-06 dock procedure and the summer extension notice (+21 days for orders delivered 2026-07-15 to 2026-08-15). The spring notice and the 2025 policy have ended, so I ignored them.\n\n**Refunded (20, status `resolved`):**\n- Tickets: 1402, 1403, 1404, 1406, 1409, 1413, 1414, 1416, 1417, 1421, 1422, 1424, 1426, 1428, 1429, 1431, 1432, 1433, 1434, 1436.\n- Ticket 1402 was already cleared at the dock, so I only added the comment and status.\n- Tickets 1417 and 1424 are defective, so I wrote the units off with `damage` adjustments.\n- The rest I restocked, each in the candidate warehouse with the fewest units at that moment.\n\n**Not refundable (5, status `closed`):**\n- 1412, 1420, 1427 and 1437: `return window expired`.\n- 1418: `final sale` (HG-3105 is discontinued and the unit was opened).\n- I moved no stock for these, so their units stay in `returns`.\n\n**Awaiting return (2, status `pending`):**\n- 1415: 2 of 3 units received.\n- 1435: 0 of 1 units received.\n\nI did not verify the final stock levels after the moves.","final_output":"I settled all 27 open refund tickets in id order, and a final search shows none left open. /app/STATUS.json is written with statu